# Response headers for static assets, applied by Cloudflare Workers Assets.
#
# This is the mechanism rather than next.config.ts's headers() for one reason: Cache-Control
# on an asset is set by the asset server, and a value from headers() does not displace it.
# Permissions-Policy does arrive from next.config (it is on every asset response in
# production), which is why that one is in both places and this file is not the only copy.

# Next's own build output. Safe at a year because the filename contains a content hash, so
# an upgrade is a different URL rather than the same URL with different bytes.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public,max-age=31536000,immutable

# Vendored runtimes: MediaPipe's selfie segmenter (~19 MB on disk, 2.7 MB brotli for the
# WASM alone), onnxruntime for in-browser captions (~31 MB) and rnnoise (~380 KB). See the
# README in each directory for why they are served from this origin at all.
#
# They were on the asset server's default of `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`, which
# means the browser may not use its own copy without asking first. Each of these is fetched
# lazily — MediaPipe when somebody picks a background, onnxruntime when captions start — so
# the cost was a conditional request per asset on every session that used the feature, and a
# full re-download of 2.7 MB whenever a cache entry had been evicted in between. For files
# that have not changed since they were vendored, that is a round trip bought for nothing.
#
# Thirty days rather than a year, and deliberately WITHOUT `immutable`, which is the whole
# decision here. Unlike /_next/static above, these paths carry no version or content hash:
# public/mediapipe/README.md documents refreshing them by copying new bytes over the old
# ones at the same URL. `immutable` tells the browser not to revalidate even on an explicit
# reload, so on a path like this it would mean an upgraded runtime never reaching anyone who
# already had the old one — and no way for them to fix it but to clear their cache. Leaving
# it off keeps "reload the page" an honest remedy, and thirty days still removes the round
# trip from every session anybody actually runs.
#
# If a year is wanted later, the way to earn it is a version in the path
# (/mediapipe/0.10.14/wasm), not a longer max-age here.
/mediapipe/*
  Cache-Control: public,max-age=2592000

/onnxruntime/*
  Cache-Control: public,max-age=2592000

# MODNet for the Enhanced background on WebGPU (~25 MB). Same reasoning, same unversioned path.
/matting/*
  Cache-Control: public,max-age=2592000

/rnnoise/*
  Cache-Control: public,max-age=2592000

# The background images the picker offers. Same reasoning, same unversioned paths.
/backgrounds/*
  Cache-Control: public,max-age=2592000

/*
  Permissions-Policy: identity-credentials-get=(self "https://accounts.google.com")
